# Editor configuration.
#
# Copy this to `.env.local` (which is git-ignored) and uncomment what you want. Every line here is
# OPTIONAL: with none of them set, the editor runs entirely in your browser — projects in IndexedDB,
# no account, no server. That is the default and it is a complete product, not a degraded mode.
#
# A file is used rather than shell variables because `VITE_X=y pnpm editor` is Unix shell syntax
# that does not work in Windows cmd or PowerShell. Vite reads this automatically on any platform.

# The platform API: accounts, cloud projects, asset uploads.
# Needs Postgres and `pnpm --filter @helaengine/api start`.
# VITE_API_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:3000

# Real-time collaboration. Only does anything when VITE_API_ORIGIN is set too, because a room is a
# *cloud* project — one stored only in this browser has nobody to share it with.
# Needs `pnpm --filter @helaengine/collab-server start`.
# VITE_COLLAB_ORIGIN=ws://127.0.0.1:3200

# The share service, for turning a validated export into a link.
# Needs `pnpm --filter @helaengine/share start`.
# VITE_SHARE_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:4000
